+## Re-run with the DetailMap PBR routes
+
+The Release audit was repeated after patches 2448–2451 added PBR routing for
+`DetailMapMaterial`, `Masked2DetailMapMaterial`, `IllumDetailMapMaterial`, and
+`DetailMap2Dm1Msk2PassMaterial`:
+
+```text
+DetailMap2Dm1Msk2PassMaterial: 2 production pipelines created.
+DetailMapMaterial: 8 production pipelines created.
+DetailMapMaterial_Skinned: 8 production pipelines created.
+IllumDetailMapMaterial: 2 production pipelines created.
+Masked2DetailMapMaterial: 2 production pipelines created.
+PBR: 1024 production pipelines created.
+PBR_Skinned: 1024 production pipelines created.
+SDL_GPU production pipeline audit passed: 26 bundles, 3495 pipelines created and released.
+```
+
+This confirms production pipeline creation for the newly routed material types
+alongside the main PBR variants. It still does not draw those materials or
+verify their pixels.
+
+A fresh OpenGL NAP-only capture attempt used the current Release build and the
+14-entry active manifest. Manifest sizes and SHA-256 values matched, and the
+`planet-hdr-profile` archive's internal version 5 matched its manifest entry.
+The process stopped after `SDL: Using SDL3`, before OpenGL initialization or
+game-data loading, and produced no screenshot. Visual acceptance remains open.
+`strace` places the wait in the Wayland window setup: SDL connected to
+`/run/user/1000/wayland-0`, sent its initial request, and then polled that
+socket without receiving a reply. Setting
+`SDL_VIDEO_WAYLAND_ALLOW_LIBDECOR=0` did not change the wait. An Xwayland
+`glxinfo -B` query with the active Xauthority file also timed out, and an
+SDL-offscreen OpenGL attempt likewise did not reach GL initialization. This
+evidence places the current capture blocker before scene rendering; it does
+not establish a shader or material failure.
+
+## Follow-up display probes
+
+On 2026-10-19, the same NAP-only Hi02 capture was retried from the exact staged
+application directory with isolated XDG state and the verified 14-package
+manifest. Native Wayland again stopped after the engine version line and was
+terminated at 150 seconds. The log still had no OpenGL renderer or game-data
+initialization.
+
+An SDL offscreen retry with `EGL_PLATFORM=surfaceless` also stopped at the same
+startup point. Mesa could not load the forced `llvmpipe` DRI module by that
+name; no image was written. A nested `Xephyr :92` probe could not connect to
+the current Xwayland `:0`, and `xdpyinfo` against `:0` timed out with the active
+Xauthority file. The Xephyr process was stopped without changing the desktop
+session. These probes do not test scene rendering. A working X server or
+compositor response is still needed for fixed-camera PBR/HDR visual acceptance.
